 sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User
    participant Browser as Portfolio Advisor (Dashboard)
    participant Backend as Node.js Backend & LLM
    participant Files as Filesystem (investment_thesis.md & target_portfolio.json)

    Note over User, Files: Scenario: Quarterly Portfolio Check — thesis-agnostic flow

    User->>Browser: Opens Portfolio Advisor (Passive View)
    Browser->>Backend: GET /api/theses/target-portfolio/health

    Backend->>Files: Read target_portfolio.json (pillar targets + holdings)
    Files-->>Backend: Return active thesis (name, pillars, holdings, target weights)
    Backend->>Backend: Fetch live prices via yfinance / Questrade sync
    Backend->>Backend: Calculate drift per pillar (targetPct − actualPct)
    Backend-->>Browser: Return ThesisHealth { thesisName, pillars[], holdingHealth[], alerts[] }

    Browser-->>User: Display pillar drift bars + Current % / Target % columns in table

    User->>Browser: Clicks "Investment Thesis" button
    Browser->>Backend: GET /api/docs/investment-thesis
    Backend->>Files: Read investment_thesis.md + thesis name from target_portfolio.json
    Files-->>Backend: Return { content, thesisName, thesisDescription }
    Backend-->>Browser: Return thesis markdown + live metadata
    Browser-->>User: Modal: renders thesis name + description from API (not hardcoded)

    User->>Browser: Clicks "Latest Review" button
    Browser->>Backend: GET /api/docs/latest-review-data
    Backend->>Files: Scan PortfolioAnalysis/strategic-reviews/ — pick newest YYYY-MM-DD*.json
    Files-->>Backend: Return structured review { holdings[], pillars[], overallScore, status }
    Backend-->>Browser: Return review JSON
    Browser-->>User: Modal: Current % vs Recommended % per holding, action/urgency/rationale

    User->>Browser: Clicks "Optimize Portfolio" (Active)

    Note right of Browser: BROWSER NEVER TALKS TO LLM
    Browser->>Backend: POST /api/theses/target-portfolio/optimize (drift data)

    Backend->>Backend: Build prompt (system: "You are Portfolio Balancer" + drift + prices + thesis name)

    Note right of Backend: Uses configured LLM SDK (model-agnostic)
    Backend->>LLM: model.generateContent(prompt)
    LLM-->>Backend: Return JSON { "trades": [{ "buy": "INTC", "amount": 1000 }] }

    Backend-->>Browser: Return action plan
    Browser-->>User: Modal: "Buy $1000 INTC to restore drift alignment. Execute?"
